{"level":20,"time":1767423372331,"pid":23601,"hostname":"liangweijiedeMacBook-Pro.local","msg":"[LlmCoTPolicy] State: {\"currentTitle\":\"Abd al-Ilah\",\"summary\":\"Abd al-Ilah of Hejaz (Arabic: عبد الإله بن علي الهاشمي)  (Arabic: عبد الإله; also written Abdul Ilah or Abdullah; 14 November 1913 – 14 July 1958) was a cousin and brother-in-law of King Ghazi of the Hashemite Kingdom of Iraq and was regent for his nephew King Faisal II, from 4 April 1939 to 23 May 1953, when Faisal came of age. Abd al-Ilah also held the title of Crown Prince of Iraq from 1943 to 1953.\\nAbd al-Ilah was killed along with the rest of the Iraqi royal family in the 14 July Revolution in 1958 that ended the Hashemite monarchy in Iraq. His body was mutilated, dragged across the streets of Baghdad, and eventually burnt.\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abd%20al-Ilah\",\"goal\":\"French Revolution\",\"history\":[\"American Revolution\",\"14 July Revolution\",\"Abd al-Ilah\"],\"depth\":3,\"links\":[\"'Abd al-Ilah\",\"14 July Revolution\",\"1941 Iraqi coup d'état\",\"Abd Allah ibn Hasan\",\"Abd al-Muttalib\",\"Abdul-Karim Qasim\",\"Abdullah II of Jordan\",\"Abdullah I of Jordan\",\"Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib\",\"Abu Numayy I\",\"Abu Numayy II\",\"Abu Sa'd al-Hasan\",\"Abu Talib ibn Abd al-Muttalib\",\"Ajlan ibn Rumaythah\",\"Al-Rashid Street (Iraq)\",\"Al-Rehab Palace\",\"Alan Lennox-Boyd, 1st Viscount Boyd of Merton\",\"Ali\",\"Ali bin Hussein, King of Hejaz\",\"Ali of Hejaz\",\"Aliya bint Ali\",\"Allies of World War II\",\"Amman\",\"Anglo-Iraqi War\",\"Arab Federation\",\"Arabic language\",\"Baghdad\",\"Barakat ibn Hasan\",\"Bess Truman\",\"Cecil Beaton\",\"Central Treaty Organization\",\"Con Coughlin\",\"Coup d'état\",\"Crown Prince\",\"Crown Prince of Jordan\",\"Crown prince\",\"Doi (identifier)\",\"Dynasty\",\"Embassy of the United States, Baghdad\",\"Emirate of Transjordan\",\"Faisal I\",\"Faisal II\",\"Faisal I of Iraq\",\"Farouk of Egypt\",\"Fatimah\",\"Field marshal\",\"First