{"level":30,"time":1767423394701,"pid":23601,"hostname":"liangweijiedeMacBook-Pro.local","msg":"[LlmCoTPolicy] LLM Response: {\n  \"reasoning\": \"The current article is a broad survey of Chinese history; the goal is the French Revolution, a major event in European and world history. From a global-history overview like this, the most efficient path is to move to an article that covers world or regional (European) history, or at least non-Chinese history, where the French Revolution is central. Among the visible links, most are China- or Taiwan-specific. The one that clearly shifts scope toward global/European context is \\\"Age of Discovery\\\", a major period in early modern European expansion that is often discussed alongside later European developments, including the Enlightenment and the French Revolution, and is likely to link to European history overviews that in turn link directly to the French Revolution. Therefore, \\\"Age of Discovery\\\" is the best available step toward the French Revolution from this page.\",\n  \"selected_link\": \"Age of Discovery\"\n}"}
